ion. The voice dictation is incredibly fast and productive, but nobody wants to speak to their computer when they're in public or around other people. So we built a way to keep the speed of speaking without making a sound. So vocal detects subtle movements in your speech muscles and turns them into text at over 200 words per minute. Our glasses send radar signals through your face, as you silently form words, tiny movements in your speech muscles, change how those signals bounce back, how our AI learns from these signals and turns them into text. So now you can control your computer without typing or speaking out loud. Ask your AI anything, write messages or get things done without anyone around you knows. And it's not just for talking to computers, you can even have a private conversation with someone else who's wearing subvocal. Even from across a crowded room without anyone hearing a word. We believe the future of internet, and computers, AI agents will be silent, seamless and far faster than what exists today. And we're building that future.", "language": "en", "model": "tiny"}